                "subject_type": "symbol",
                "subject_id": "mcp-server/src/tools/findings.ts:requireAncestor",
                "statement": "verify_finding_fix's lineage check separates the two ways it can decline. `requireAncestor` branches on the exit status of `git merge-base --is-ancestor`: 0 returns, 1 refuses because the verification evidence genuinely predates or sits outside the repair lineage, and any other status refuses with a distinct message carrying git's own stderr. Because the second and third branches are never merged, a repository the server cannot read produces \"cannot compare repair and evidence commits\" rather than the lineage refusal — and neither produces a pass. The check has no path on which an unanswerable question is recorded as an answer.",
